{"name":"Philippine Yellow","hex":"#fecb00","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"philippine","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Alternative spelling of Philippine."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/philippine"},{"term":"yellow","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of sunflower petals and lemons; the color obtained by mixing green and red light, or by subtracting blue from white light; the color evoked by light of wavelength around 580 nm; one of the three primary colors in subtractive color systems.","The middle light in a set of three traffic lights, the lighting of which indicates that drivers should stop short of the intersection if it is safe to do so."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a yellow hue.","Lacking courage."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/yellow"}],"entries":[{"title":"Philippines","blocks":[{"text":"The Philippines, officially the Republic of the Philippines, is an archipelagic country in Southeast Asia. Located in the western Pacific Ocean, it consists of about 7,641 islands, with a total area of about 300,000 square kilometers. The islands are broadly categorized into three main geographical divisions: from north to south, Luzon, Visayas, and Mindanao. With a population of over 114 million, it is the world's thirteenth-most-populous country."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/99/Flag_of_the_Philippines.svg/330px-Flag_of_the_Philippines.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Philippines","wikidata":"Q928"},{"title":"Yellow","blocks":[{"text":"Yellow is a color between green and orange on the spectrum of light. It is evoked by light with a dominant wavelength of roughly 575–585 nm. It is a primary color in subtractive color systems, used in painting or color printing. In the RGB color model, used to create colors on television and computer screens, yellow is a secondary color made by combining red and green at equal intensity. Carotenoids give the characteristic yellow color to autumn leaves, corn, canaries, daffodils, and lemons, as well as egg yolks, buttercups, and bananas. They absorb light energy and protect plants from photo damage in some cases. Sunlight has a slight yellowish hue when the Sun is near the horizon, due to atmospheric scattering of shorter wavelengths."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d5/Cornwall_Daffodils.jpg/330px-Cornwall_Daffodils.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yellow","wikidata":"Q943"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/Manunggul_Jar.jpg/500px-Manunggul_Jar.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/Manunggul_Jar.jpg/1280px-Manunggul_Jar.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/Manunggul_Jar.jpg/500px-Manunggul_Jar.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Manunggul burial jar, one of the numerous burial jars found on the cave system","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AManunggul_Jar.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/Naturales_4.png/500px-Naturales_4.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/Naturales_4.png/500px-Naturales_4.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A couple portrayed in 1590's Early Spanish colonial period of the Philippines, draped in gold","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANaturales_4.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/44/Vista_del_Puente_de_Mani